.nh
.TH "PB-ENV-REMOVE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-remove - Remove this machine's local ENV vault custody


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env remove [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove this machine's local ENV vault custody

.PP
Remove this machine's local vault custody after exact confirmation. This differs from reset: account ENV values and other authorized machines are not deleted.

.PP
ENV values are encrypted before they leave the client. The interactive picker separates shared Team globals, your private member globals, and device overrides in the active workspace; commands select exact scopes explicitly; list output shows metadata rather than secret values. Unlock the local vault when a key operation requires it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	exact confirmation phrase: REMOVE LOCAL ENV <account_id>

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for remove

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP
